From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] winex11: a child window whose kept Vulkan frame was dropped is asked to paint again

A child window that presents with Vulkan has its last frame kept and shown
again over GDI (SG 1523). When its top-level is resized, shown or hidden,
that frame is dropped, because it is no longer where it was. The window then
showed what GDI had there until the program presented again on its own:
after Restore Down, Excel's Name Box and the formula bar buttons stayed a
blank white box with a black border until clicked. Such a window is now
asked to paint again, which presents a new frame.
---
diff --git a/dlls/winex11.drv/vulkan.c b/dlls/winex11.drv/vulkan.c
index cfd071c..3a92cee 100644
--- a/dlls/winex11.drv/vulkan.c
+++ b/dlls/winex11.drv/vulkan.c
@@ -193,6 +193,16 @@ void vulkan_surfaces_window_changed( HWND hwnd )
             surface->shown_on = 0;
         }
         pthread_mutex_unlock( &shown_mutex );
+
+        /* Stained Glass OS: a window whose frame is no longer shown is asked to paint again, which
+         * presents a new one. Kept off, it showed what GDI had there until the program presented on
+         * its own: Excel's Name Box and formula buttons stayed a blank white box after Restore
+         * Down, Word's ribbon black after a popup closed, until the mouse went over them. */
+#ifndef SG_MUTANT_VK_CHANGED_NO_REPAINT
+        for (i = 0; i < count; i++)
+            if (NtUserIsWindowVisible( gone[i] ))
+                NtUserRedrawWindow( gone[i], NULL, 0, RDW_INVALIDATE | RDW_ALLCHILDREN );
+#endif
     }
     free( hwnds );
 }
